### Nuclear Weapons — the deterrence half, as a type library: one type per
### section (te_nuclear_sec_*) for je_nuclear_program ("Nuclear Weapons"),
### which since 2026-09-25 carries posture and crises as well as the programme.
### gui/journal_entry_widgets/nuclear_layout_widget.gui sets the order of these
### sections among the programme half's (nuclear_program_widget.gui) and holds
### the named roots the entry attaches; see its header for the whole panel.
###
### te_nuclear_sec_crisis       The live crisis (open, only while there is
###                             one): a headline (the opponent, our side, the
###                             dispute), the readings as a grid of cells
###                             (stage, deadline, danger, pressure,
###                             follow-through, the next pressure), Our Moves,
###                             then what each outcome brings (NUC-7).
### te_nuclear_sec_world_crises Every crisis in the world, ours included
###                             (open, only while there is one): a datamodel
###                             over nd_crises, one row each with both flags,
###                             most dangerous first, details on hover
###                             (nd_world_crisis_item_detail_sgui; NUC-14).
### te_nuclear_sec_posture      Doctrine, readiness and launch authority, one
###                             row each with a Change toggle that opens its
###                             choices beneath it (readiness as a table), then
###                             the umbrella, loose warheads, upkeep and
###                             incident exposure (open, only while armed).
### te_nuclear_sec_forces       Survivability, reliability, strain, the chance
###                             a sequence is halted, the investment steppers
###                             and the arsenal's size, its count with it
###                             (open, only while armed).
### te_nuclear_sec_home         How each interest group receives the posture
###                             (open, only while armed): one small table per
###                             group with a view (nd_home_ig_table).
### te_nuclear_sec_reputation   The last crisis between crises, then our
###                             pledges once there is a record (open).
### The explanations these sections used to carry (the At Home legend, the
### crisis moves' note, the reputation note) are in "How Nuclear Weapons Work"
### (te_nuclear_sec_how, nuclear_layout_widget.gui).
###
### Design: docs/systems/nuclear_crisis_design.md (§0 is what shipped); the
### panel is described in docs/systems/journal_entry_systems.md, "Nuclear
### Deterrence Widget".
###
### WHERE THE NUMBERS COME FROM. Nothing here computes anything. Every number
### is a display script value (nd_display_* and friends in
### common/script_values/nuclear_deterrence_values.txt), every word that
### depends on state is a customizable-localization block in
### common/customizable_localization/nuclear_deterrence_custom_loc.txt, and the
### incident band is projected into nd_risk_band in script. No threshold is
### restated in this file.
###
### WHAT A HUMAN CAN DO HERE. Two action handlers in
### common/scripted_guis/nuclear_deterrence_sguis.txt, addressed by op code
### (keep this table, the sgui header and journal_entry_systems.md in step):
###   nd_posture_sgui         11..15 doctrine 1..5   20..23 readiness 0..3
###                           31..34 authority 1..4  40/41 safeguards -/+
###                           50/51 hardening -/+
###                           60/61 arsenal ceiling -/+  62 lift it
###                           63 dismantle the arsenal  64 halt it
###   nd_crisis_action_sgui   1 go public  2 propose stand-down  3 exercise
###                           4 concede    5 let it go
### The AI does not use these (ai_is_valid = no): it sets its posture in
### nd_ai_review_posture and answers crises through the crisis events, which
### call the same effects. Every action row sets its handler as its own
### datacontext, and test_nuclear_deterrence.gui_ops reads the op codes that
### way, counting only an op scope (AddScope( 'op', ... )): the code that tints
### the option in force is not an op.
###
### NO ACTION BUTTON'S `visible` COMES FROM AN op-BRANCHING IsShown
### (gui_modding_guide.md gotcha #22). The buttons are always drawn while their
### section is; is_valid greys them and says why. The yes/no questions this
### file does ask (armed? in a crisis? a last crisis to report? which side of
### the crisis are we on?) go to scope-free display handlers — the crisis move
### rows a side cannot make are hidden that way (nd_crisis_we_issued_sgui,
### nd_crisis_we_are_target_sgui, nd_crisis_private_sgui, nd_armed_sgui), and
### the pressure and danger breakdowns and the next-pressure line are
### script-built text from display handlers (nd_crisis_*_breakdown_sgui,
### nd_crisis_next_pressure_sgui, nd_risk_breakdown_sgui).
###
### The named roots that wrap these sections are gated on
### JournalEntry.IsActive (gotcha #14).
###
### Section collapse state lives in GetVariableSystem: client-side, never
### saved, invisible to script. Each flag says its default (style guide rule
### 7): *_closed sections are open until closed, *_open ones collapsed until
### opened (test_nuclear_layout.py).

### The panel's type sizes (style guide rule 3, the owner's ladder of
### 2026-10-17): rows, values, buttons and notes at 17, subheadings at 20, and
### the overview at 16 in the tooltip face. Every nuclear widget file reads
### these, so a pass on type edits numbers here, not every textbox. Templates
### are global; they sit in this file because it is the first of the four
### the engine loads (nuclear_deterrence < _layout < _overview < _program).
### test_nuclear_layout.py's LabelBudgetTest reads the sizes from here.
template te_nuclear_fontsize_row {
	fontsize = 17
}

template te_nuclear_fontsize_heading {
	fontsize = 20
}

template te_nuclear_fontsize_overview {
	fontsize = 16
	using = tooltip_font
}

types nuclear_deterrence_widget_types
{
	type nd_panel = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		parentanchor = hcenter
		spacing = 1
		margin = { 10 6 }

		background = {
			using = entry_bg_fancy_dark
			alpha = 0.5
		}
	}

	type nd_section_header = section_header_button {
		blockoverride "layout" {
			parentanchor = hcenter
			size = { 520 38 }
		}
	}

	type nd_text = textbox {
		autoresize = yes
		multiline = yes
		minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
		maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
		align = left|nobaseline
		using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
	}

	### A label/value line with one tooltip for the whole row.
	type nd_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4
		margin = { 6 1 }

		block "row_tooltip" {}

		textbox = {
			size = { 210 24 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
			parentanchor = vcenter
			elide = right
			alwaystransparent = yes
			### Underlined, since the row carries a tooltip (style rule 3). A row
			### without one overrides this block empty.
			block "label_format" {
				default_format = "#tooltippable"
			}
			block "row_label" {}
		}

		textbox = {
			size = { 266 24 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
			parentanchor = vcenter
			elide = right
			alwaystransparent = yes
			block "row_value" {}
		}
	}

	### A choice: its name and one action button, in a row 480 wide (6 + 358
	### + 6 + 110). The name says what the option is on hover (underlined;
	### a row whose name has no hover overrides "name_format" empty); the
	### button says why it is greyed and what pressing it does. The option in
	### force is tinted, as Covert's Funding Levels table does: the instance's
	### "row_current" sets the tint's visible. The instance sets the row's
	### datacontext (its handler), the name in "choice_name" and the button's
	### text and binding.
	type nd_choice_row = widget {
		size = { 480 32 }

		icon = {
			size = { 100% 100% }
			texture = "gfx/interface/backgrounds/white.dds"
			color = { 0.9 0.75 0.35 0.2 }
			block "row_current" {
				visible = no
			}
		}
		flowcontainer = {
			direction = horizontal
			ignoreinvisible = yes
			spacing = 6
			position = { 6 0 }
			parentanchor = vcenter

			textbox = {
				size = { 358 30 }
				align = left|nobaseline
				using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
				parentanchor = vcenter
				elide = right
				block "name_format" {
					default_format = "#tooltippable"
				}
				block "choice_name" {}
			}
			button = {
				using = default_button_action
				size = { 110 30 }
				parentanchor = vcenter
				block "button_text" {}
				block "button_binding" {}
			}
		}
	}

	### One axis of the posture (style guide rules 3 and 6): the axis, a
	### concept, so hovering the word explains the term; what is in force,
	### underlined, its hover saying what it does now and when it can next
	### change; and a toggle beside it that opens the axis's choices directly
	### beneath (6 + 160 + 4 + 218 + 4 + 90 + 6 = 488, an nd_row's width).
	### The label is not alwaystransparent, or the concept could not hover.
	type nd_axis_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4
		margin = { 6 2 }

		textbox = {
			size = { 160 30 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
			parentanchor = vcenter
			elide = right
			block "axis_label" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			size = { 218 30 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
			parentanchor = vcenter
			elide = right
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			block "axis_value" {}
		}
		button = {
			using = default_button
			size = { 90 30 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			block "axis_toggle" {}
		}
	}

	### The readiness levels as a comparison table (NUC-5): the level (its
	### hover says what it is, in modifier lines), what the deterrent would
	### cost a week there, the survivability a crisis would count there, and
	### the Order button. 6 + 120 + 6 + 100 + 6 + 124 + 6 + 110 = 478. The level
	### ordered is tinted, as a choice row's option in force is.
	type nd_readiness_row = widget {
		size = { 480 32 }

		icon = {
			size = { 100% 100% }
			texture = "gfx/interface/backgrounds/white.dds"
			color = { 0.9 0.75 0.35 0.2 }
			block "row_current" {
				visible = no
			}
		}
		flowcontainer = {
			direction = horizontal
			ignoreinvisible = yes
			spacing = 6
			position = { 6 0 }
			parentanchor = vcenter

			textbox = {
				size = { 120 30 }
				align = left|nobaseline
				using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
				parentanchor = vcenter
				elide = right
				default_format = "#tooltippable"
				block "level_name" {}
			}
			textbox = {
				size = { 100 30 }
				align = right|nobaseline
				using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
				parentanchor = vcenter
				elide = right
				alwaystransparent = yes
				block "level_upkeep" {}
			}
			textbox = {
				size = { 124 30 }
				align = right|nobaseline
				using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
				parentanchor = vcenter
				elide = right
				alwaystransparent = yes
				block "level_survivability" {}
			}
			button = {
				using = default_button_action
				size = { 110 30 }
				parentanchor = vcenter
				block "button_text" {}
				block "button_binding" {}
			}
		}
	}

	### The readiness table's column heads, in the rows' cells; each head with
	### a hover says what its column counts.
	type nd_readiness_head = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 6
		margin = { 6 1 }

		textbox = {
			size = { 120 24 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
			parentanchor = vcenter
			elide = right
			default_format = "#lore"
			text = "nd_w_readiness_head_level"
		}
		textbox = {
			size = { 100 24 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
			parentanchor = vcenter
			elide = right
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			text = "nd_w_readiness_head_upkeep"
			tooltip = "nd_w_readiness_head_upkeep_tt"
		}
		textbox = {
			size = { 124 24 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
			parentanchor = vcenter
			elide = right
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			text = "nd_w_readiness_head_survivability"
			tooltip = "nd_w_readiness_head_survivability_tt"
		}
	}

	### A reading of the live crisis (NUC-7), in the overview cell's shape
	### (te_banking_ov_cell) without its icon: the caption, the word and a
	### figure, in a 218 column at the row size. The instance sets the size
	### (238 x 70 with a figure, 238 x 48 without), its tooltip (the reading's
	### breakdown), "caption", "word" and, where it has one, "figure".
	type nd_crisis_cell = widget {
		size = { 238 70 }

		background = {
			using = entry_bg_simple
		}

		textbox = {
			position = { 10 2 }
			autoresize = yes
			max_width = 218
			elide = right
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			block "caption" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			position = { 10 24 }
			autoresize = yes
			max_width = 218
			elide = right
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
			block "word" {}
		}
		block "figure" {}
	}

	type nd_crisis_cell_figure = textbox {
		position = { 10 46 }
		autoresize = yes
		max_width = 218
		elide = right
		align = left|nobaseline
		using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
	}

	### A row of the crisis's Outcomes: the outcome, what it brings, and the
	### change to our credibility (6 + 170 + 4 + 192 + 4 + 104 = 480).
	type nd_outcome_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4
		margin = { 6 1 }

		block "row_tooltip" {}

		textbox = {
			size = { 170 24 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
			parentanchor = vcenter
			elide = right
			alwaystransparent = yes
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			block "outcome_label" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			size = { 192 24 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
			parentanchor = vcenter
			elide = right
			alwaystransparent = yes
			block "outcome_effect" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			size = { 104 24 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
			parentanchor = vcenter
			elide = right
			alwaystransparent = yes
			block "outcome_credibility" {}
		}
	}

	### The Outcomes table's column heads, in its rows' cells.
	type nd_outcome_head = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4
		margin = { 6 1 }

		textbox = {
			size = { 170 24 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
			parentanchor = vcenter
			elide = right
			default_format = "#lore"
			text = "nd_w_crisis_outcomes_head_outcome"
		}
		textbox = {
			size = { 192 24 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
			parentanchor = vcenter
			elide = right
			default_format = "#lore"
			text = "nd_w_crisis_outcomes_head_effect"
		}
		textbox = {
			size = { 104 24 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
			parentanchor = vcenter
			elide = right
			default_format = "#lore"
			text = "nd_w_crisis_outcomes_head_credibility"
		}
	}

	### A funding-style stepper row: label, [-] value [+].
	type nd_stepper_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4
		margin = { 6 2 }
	}

	### A line built in script (a country's name out of a variable). A line
	### with a hover sets its tooltip and underline in "line_format".
	type nd_script_line = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		parentanchor = hcenter
		margin = { 6 1 }

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			multiline = yes
			minimumsize = { 468 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 468 -1 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
			block "line_format" {}
			block "line_text" {}
		}
	}

	### ---- At Home: one table per interest group -------------------------------
	### Round 3 (the owner's review, 2026-09-30): each group with a view of our
	### posture is a small table, its name and class over a row for its approval
	### and a row for each term behind it, in place of two lines of script-built
	### text. The tables are the items of a datamodel over the country's groups
	### (te_nuclear_sec_home), so the item's datacontext is the InterestGroup and
	### every number is an nd_disp_ig_* value read through
	### InterestGroup.MakeScope.ScriptValue (vanilla's own chain,
	### NEGOTIATE_LAW_SUCCESS_CHANCE_INCREASE). A tooltip on a datamodel item
	### renders with that item's context alone (gui_modding_guide.md gotcha #24),
	### so the tooltips here are static text. These types sit above the first
	### action row: their (CFixedPoint) literals are not op codes.

	### A row of a group's table: the term, and what it does to the group's
	### approval. Fixed cells (220 + 60), indented under the group's name.
	type nd_home_term_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		margin_left = 24
		block "row_tooltip" {}

		textbox = {
			size = { 220 22 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
			parentanchor = vcenter
			elide = right
			block "label_format" {
				default_format = "#tooltippable"
			}
			block "row_label" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			size = { 60 22 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
			parentanchor = vcenter
			elide = right
			block "row_value" {}
		}
	}

	### One group's table: drawn only for a group with a view (nd_disp_ig_class
	### is 0 for one without). Its rows are its class's terms, as the text
	### list's lines were (nd_disp_ig_shows_*).
	type nd_home_ig_table = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 1
		visible = "[NotEqualTo_CFixedPoint( InterestGroup.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nd_disp_ig_class'), '(CFixedPoint)0' )]"

		### The group, and how it judges us (280 + 200).
		flowcontainer = {
			direction = horizontal
			ignoreinvisible = yes

			textbox = {
				size = { 280 24 }
				align = left|nobaseline
				using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
				parentanchor = vcenter
				elide = right
				text = "nd_home_ig_name"
			}
			widget = {
				size = { 200 24 }
				parentanchor = vcenter

				textbox = {
					size = { 200 24 }
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( InterestGroup.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nd_disp_ig_view'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
					align = right|nobaseline
					using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
					parentanchor = vcenter
					default_format = "#lore"
					text = "nd_home_view_1"
				}
				textbox = {
					size = { 200 24 }
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( InterestGroup.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nd_disp_ig_view'), '(CFixedPoint)2' )]"
					align = right|nobaseline
					using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
					parentanchor = vcenter
					default_format = "#lore"
					text = "nd_home_view_2"
				}
				textbox = {
					size = { 200 24 }
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( InterestGroup.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nd_disp_ig_view'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
					align = right|nobaseline
					using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
					parentanchor = vcenter
					default_format = "#lore"
					text = "nd_home_view_3"
				}
				textbox = {
					size = { 200 24 }
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( InterestGroup.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nd_disp_ig_view'), '(CFixedPoint)4' )]"
					align = right|nobaseline
					using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
					parentanchor = vcenter
					default_format = "#lore"
					text = "nd_home_view_4"
				}
				textbox = {
					size = { 200 24 }
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( InterestGroup.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nd_disp_ig_view'), '(CFixedPoint)5' )]"
					align = right|nobaseline
					using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
					parentanchor = vcenter
					default_format = "#lore"
					text = "nd_home_view_5"
				}
				textbox = {
					size = { 200 24 }
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( InterestGroup.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nd_disp_ig_view'), '(CFixedPoint)6' )]"
					align = right|nobaseline
					using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
					parentanchor = vcenter
					default_format = "#lore"
					text = "nd_home_view_6"
				}
				textbox = {
					size = { 200 24 }
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( InterestGroup.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nd_disp_ig_view'), '(CFixedPoint)7' )]"
					align = right|nobaseline
					using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
					parentanchor = vcenter
					default_format = "#lore"
					text = "nd_home_view_7"
				}
				textbox = {
					size = { 200 24 }
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( InterestGroup.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nd_disp_ig_view'), '(CFixedPoint)8' )]"
					align = right|nobaseline
					using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
					parentanchor = vcenter
					default_format = "#lore"
					text = "nd_home_view_8"
				}
				textbox = {
					size = { 200 24 }
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( InterestGroup.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nd_disp_ig_view'), '(CFixedPoint)9' )]"
					align = right|nobaseline
					using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
					parentanchor = vcenter
					default_format = "#lore"
					text = "nd_home_view_9"
				}
				textbox = {
					size = { 200 24 }
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( InterestGroup.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nd_disp_ig_view'), '(CFixedPoint)10' )]"
					align = right|nobaseline
					using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
					parentanchor = vcenter
					default_format = "#lore"
					text = "nd_home_view_10"
				}
			}
		}
		nd_home_term_row = {
			blockoverride "row_tooltip" {
				tooltip = "nd_home_row_approval_tt"
			}
			blockoverride "row_label" {
				text = "nd_home_row_approval"
			}
			blockoverride "row_value" {
				text = "nd_home_row_approval_value"
			}
		}
		nd_home_term_row = {
			visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( InterestGroup.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nd_disp_ig_shows_doctrine'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
			blockoverride "row_tooltip" {
				tooltip = "nd_home_row_doctrine_tt"
			}
			blockoverride "row_label" {
				text = "nd_home_row_doctrine"
			}
			blockoverride "row_value" {
				text = "nd_home_row_doctrine_value"
			}
		}
		nd_home_term_row = {
			visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( InterestGroup.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nd_disp_ig_shows_readiness'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
			blockoverride "row_tooltip" {
				tooltip = "nd_home_row_readiness_tt"
			}
			blockoverride "row_label" {
				text = "nd_home_row_readiness"
			}
			blockoverride "row_value" {
				text = "nd_home_row_readiness_value"
			}
		}
		nd_home_term_row = {
			visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( InterestGroup.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nd_disp_ig_shows_authority'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
			blockoverride "row_tooltip" {
				tooltip = "nd_home_row_authority_tt"
			}
			blockoverride "row_label" {
				text = "nd_home_row_authority"
			}
			blockoverride "row_value" {
				text = "nd_home_row_authority_value"
			}
		}
		nd_home_term_row = {
			visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( InterestGroup.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nd_disp_ig_shows_strain'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
			blockoverride "row_tooltip" {
				tooltip = "nd_home_row_strain_tt"
			}
			blockoverride "row_label" {
				text = "nd_home_row_strain"
			}
			blockoverride "row_value" {
				text = "nd_home_row_strain_value"
			}
		}
		nd_home_term_row = {
			visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( InterestGroup.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nd_disp_ig_shows_possession'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
			blockoverride "row_tooltip" {
				tooltip = "nd_home_row_possession_tt"
			}
			blockoverride "row_label" {
				text = "nd_home_row_possession"
			}
			blockoverride "row_value" {
				text = "nd_home_row_possession_value"
			}
		}
		nd_home_term_row = {
			visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( InterestGroup.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nd_disp_ig_shows_business'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
			blockoverride "row_tooltip" {
				tooltip = "nd_home_row_business_tt"
			}
			blockoverride "row_label" {
				text = "nd_home_row_business"
			}
			blockoverride "row_value" {
				text = "nd_home_row_business_value"
			}
		}
		nd_home_term_row = {
			visible = "[NotEqualTo_CFixedPoint( InterestGroup.MakeScope.ScriptValue('nd_disp_ig_cap_cut'), '(CFixedPoint)0' )]"
			blockoverride "row_tooltip" {
				tooltip = "nd_home_row_cap_tt"
			}
			blockoverride "row_label" {
				text = "nd_home_row_cap"
			}
			blockoverride "row_value" {
				text = "nd_home_row_cap_value"
			}
		}
	}

	### A heading inside a section's panel, over one group of its lines, with a
	### faint rule under it: un_chamber_subheader's shape (un_chamber_widget.gui),
	### under this file's prefix. Headings are GUI rows, not script-built lines
	### (gui_modding_guide.md gotcha #18).
	type nd_subheader = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 1
		block "subheader_margin" {
			margin_top = 10
		}

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			multiline = yes
			maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_heading
			default_format = "#title"
			block "subheader_text" {}
		}
		divider_clean = {
			blockoverride "size" {
				size = { 480 2 }
			}
		}
	}

	### Explanatory text under a heading in How Nuclear Weapons Work: how a
	### thing works, rather than what it says now (un_chamber_note's shape).
	type nd_note = textbox {
		autoresize = yes
		multiline = yes
		minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
		maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
		align = left|nobaseline
		using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
		default_format = "#lore"
	}

	### A collapsible subsection inside a section's panel: narrower, lower and
	### in a smaller type than nd_section_header, set in from the panel's edge
	### by the flowcontainer that holds it (un_chamber_subsection_header's
	### shape). Used for the doctrine and readiness choices under Nuclear
	### Posture, and for the taboo's chart.
	type nd_subsection_header = section_header_button {
		blockoverride "layout" {
			size = { 440 30 }
		}
		blockoverride "fontsize" {
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
		}
		blockoverride "arrow_size" {
			size = { 20 20 }
		}
		blockoverride "left_textbox_margin_left" {
			margin_left = 32
		}
	}

	### One row of World Crises (NUC-14): an item of nd_crises, so its
	### datacontext is the issuer's capital and the issuer is State.GetOwner
	### (gui_modding_guide.md gotcha #15); the target is the capital the
	### refresh stored on the issuer, nd_wc_target_cap (gotcha #11). Vanilla's
	### flags give each name on hover and open the country on a click. The row's
	### hover, rooted at the issuer, names both and gives the dispute, the clock,
	### talks, a guarantor and a private warning. A crisis of ours is tinted.
	### 6 + 40 + 4 + 20 + 4 + 40 + 8 + 160 + 6 + 180 = 468.
	type nd_world_crisis_row = widget {
		size = { 480 30 }
		tooltip = "[GetScriptedGui('nd_world_crisis_item_detail_sgui').ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( State.GetOwner.MakeScope ).End )]"

		icon = {
			size = { 100% 100% }
			texture = "gfx/interface/backgrounds/white.dds"
			color = { 0.9 0.75 0.35 0.2 }
			visible = "[Or( ObjectsEqual( State.GetOwner, GetPlayer.Self ), ObjectsEqual( State.GetOwner.MakeScope.Var('nd_wc_target_cap').GetState.GetOwner, GetPlayer.Self ) )]"
		}
		flowcontainer = {
			direction = horizontal
			ignoreinvisible = yes
			spacing = 4
			position = { 6 0 }
			parentanchor = vcenter

			widget = {
				size = { 40 28 }
				parentanchor = vcenter

				tiny_flag = {
					parentanchor = center
					datacontext = "[State.GetOwner]"
				}
			}
			textbox = {
				size = { 20 28 }
				align = center|nobaseline
				using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
				parentanchor = vcenter
				alwaystransparent = yes
				text = "nd_wc_arrow"
			}
			widget = {
				size = { 40 28 }
				parentanchor = vcenter

				tiny_flag = {
					parentanchor = center
					datacontext = "[State.GetOwner.MakeScope.Var('nd_wc_target_cap').GetState.GetOwner]"
				}
			}
			textbox = {
				size = { 168 28 }
				align = left|nobaseline
				using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
				parentanchor = vcenter
				elide = right
				alwaystransparent = yes
				default_format = "#tooltippable"
				text = "nd_wc_item_stage"
			}
			textbox = {
				size = { 180 28 }
				align = right|nobaseline
				using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
				parentanchor = vcenter
				elide = right
				alwaystransparent = yes
				text = "nd_wc_item_danger"
			}
		}
	}

	### World Crises' column heads, in its rows' cells.
	type nd_world_crisis_head = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4
		margin = { 6 1 }

		textbox = {
			size = { 108 24 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
			parentanchor = vcenter
			elide = right
			default_format = "#lore"
			text = "nd_wc_head_parties"
		}
		textbox = {
			size = { 168 24 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
			parentanchor = vcenter
			elide = right
			default_format = "#lore"
			text = "nd_wc_head_stage"
		}
		textbox = {
			size = { 180 24 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = te_nuclear_fontsize_row
			parentanchor = vcenter
			elide = right
			default_format = "#lore"
			text = "nd_wc_head_danger"
		}
	}

	### ======================================================================
	### SECTIONS. nuclear_layout_widget.gui composes them, in its order.
	### ======================================================================

	### The live crisis (open; only while there is one), compact (NUC-7): one
	### headline line (the opponent, our side, the dispute), the six readings
	### as a grid of cells two to a row (caption, word, figure; each
	### breakdown on hover), Our Moves directly under them, then what each
	### outcome would bring (the concession and our credibility). The moves a
	### side cannot make are hidden by scope-free display handlers.
	type te_nuclear_sec_crisis = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 2
		visible = "[GetScriptedGui('nd_in_crisis_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"

		nd_section_header = {
			blockoverride "left_text" {
				text = "nd_w_crisis_header"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick" {
				onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Toggle('nd_crisis_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
				visible = "[GetVariableSystem.Exists('nd_crisis_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
				visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('nd_crisis_closed'))]"
			}
		}

		nd_panel = {
			visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('nd_crisis_closed'))]"
			spacing = 4

			nd_script_line = {
				datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('nd_crisis_opponent_sgui')]"
				blockoverride "line_format" {
					default_format = "#tooltippable"
					tooltip = "nd_w_crisis_headline_tt"
				}
				blockoverride "line_text" {
					text = "[ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"
				}
			}

			### The readings: 238 + 4 + 238 = 480, two to a row.
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = horizontal
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				spacing = 4

				nd_crisis_cell = {
					size = { 238 70 }
					tooltip = "nd_w_crisis_stage_tt"
					blockoverride "caption" {
						text = "nd_w_crisis_stage_label"
					}
					blockoverride "word" {
						text = "nd_w_crisis_stage_value"
					}
					blockoverride "figure" {
						nd_crisis_cell_figure = {
							text = "nd_w_crisis_stage_figure"
						}
					}
				}
				nd_crisis_cell = {
					size = { 238 70 }
					tooltip = "nd_w_crisis_deadline_tt"
					blockoverride "caption" {
						text = "nd_w_crisis_deadline_label"
					}
					blockoverride "word" {
						text = "nd_w_crisis_deadline_value"
					}
					blockoverride "figure" {
						nd_crisis_cell_figure = {
							text = "nd_w_crisis_deadline_figure"
						}
					}
				}
			}
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = horizontal
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				spacing = 4

				nd_crisis_cell = {
					size = { 238 70 }
					tooltip = "[Concatenate( Localize( 'nd_w_crisis_danger_tt' ), GetScriptedGui('nd_crisis_danger_breakdown_sgui').ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End ) )]"
					blockoverride "caption" {
						text = "nd_w_crisis_danger_label"
					}
					blockoverride "word" {
						text = "nd_w_crisis_danger_value"
					}
					blockoverride "figure" {
						nd_crisis_cell_figure = {
							text = "nd_w_crisis_danger_figure"
						}
					}
				}
				nd_crisis_cell = {
					size = { 238 70 }
					tooltip = "[Concatenate( Localize( 'nd_w_crisis_pressure_tt' ), GetScriptedGui('nd_crisis_pressure_breakdown_sgui').ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End ) )]"
					blockoverride "caption" {
						text = "nd_w_crisis_pressure_label_value"
					}
					blockoverride "word" {
						text = "nd_w_crisis_pressure_value"
					}
					blockoverride "figure" {
						nd_crisis_cell_figure = {
							text = "nd_w_crisis_pressure_figure"
						}
					}
				}
			}
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = horizontal
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				spacing = 4

				nd_crisis_cell = {
					size = { 238 48 }
					tooltip = "nd_w_crisis_ft_tt"
					blockoverride "caption" {
						text = "nd_w_crisis_ft_label_value"
					}
					blockoverride "word" {
						text = "nd_w_crisis_ft_value"
					}
				}
				nd_crisis_cell = {
					size = { 238 48 }
					tooltip = "nd_w_crisis_next_pressure_tt"
					blockoverride "caption" {
						text = "nd_w_crisis_next_pressure_label"
					}
					blockoverride "word" {
						text = "[GetScriptedGui('nd_crisis_next_pressure_sgui').ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"
					}
				}
			}

			nd_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "nd_w_crisis_moves_sub"
				}
			}
			nd_choice_row = {
				visible = "[GetScriptedGui('nd_crisis_private_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"
				datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('nd_crisis_action_sgui')]"
				blockoverride "name_format" {}
				blockoverride "choice_name" {
					text = "nd_w_crisis_act_public"
				}
				blockoverride "button_text" {
					text = "nd_w_crisis_act_public_btn"
				}
				blockoverride "button_binding" {
					enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End )]"
					onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End ) ) )]"
				}
			}
			nd_choice_row = {
				datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('nd_crisis_action_sgui')]"
				blockoverride "name_format" {}
				blockoverride "choice_name" {
					text = "nd_w_crisis_act_talks"
				}
				blockoverride "button_text" {
					text = "nd_w_crisis_act_talks_btn"
				}
				blockoverride "button_binding" {
					enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End )]"
					onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End ) ) )]"
				}
			}
			nd_choice_row = {
				visible = "[GetScriptedGui('nd_armed_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"
				datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('nd_crisis_action_sgui')]"
				blockoverride "name_format" {}
				blockoverride "choice_name" {
					text = "nd_w_crisis_act_exercise"
				}
				blockoverride "button_text" {
					text = "nd_w_crisis_act_exercise_btn"
				}
				blockoverride "button_binding" {
					enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ).End )]"
					onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ).End ) ) )]"
				}
			}
			nd_choice_row = {
				visible = "[GetScriptedGui('nd_crisis_we_are_target_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"
				datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('nd_crisis_action_sgui')]"
				blockoverride "name_format" {}
				blockoverride "choice_name" {
					text = "nd_w_crisis_act_yield"
				}
				blockoverride "button_text" {
					text = "nd_w_crisis_act_yield_btn"
				}
				blockoverride "button_binding" {
					enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)4' ) ).End )]"
					onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)4' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)4' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)4' ) ).End ) ) )]"
				}
			}
			nd_choice_row = {
				visible = "[GetScriptedGui('nd_crisis_we_issued_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"
				datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('nd_crisis_action_sgui')]"
				blockoverride "name_format" {}
				blockoverride "choice_name" {
					text = "nd_w_crisis_act_back_down"
				}
				blockoverride "button_text" {
					text = "nd_w_crisis_act_back_down_btn"
				}
				blockoverride "button_binding" {
					enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)5' ) ).End )]"
					onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)5' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)5' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)5' ) ).End ) ) )]"
				}
			}

			### What each outcome brings (NUC-7, NUC-8): the concession, and what
			### it does to our credibility, the better outcome first for both sides.
			nd_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "nd_w_crisis_outcomes_sub"
				}
			}
			nd_outcome_head = {}
			nd_outcome_row = {
				blockoverride "row_tooltip" {
					tooltip = "nd_w_crisis_concession_tt"
				}
				blockoverride "outcome_label" {
					text = "nd_w_crisis_concede_label_value"
				}
				blockoverride "outcome_effect" {
					text = "nd_w_crisis_concession_value"
				}
				blockoverride "outcome_credibility" {
					text = "nd_w_crisis_cred_concede"
				}
			}
			nd_outcome_row = {
				blockoverride "row_tooltip" {
					tooltip = "nd_w_crisis_stakes_tt"
				}
				blockoverride "outcome_label" {
					text = "nd_w_crisis_backdown_label_value"
				}
				blockoverride "outcome_effect" {
					text = "nd_w_crisis_backdown_effect"
				}
				blockoverride "outcome_credibility" {
					text = "nd_w_crisis_cred_backdown"
				}
			}
			nd_outcome_row = {
				blockoverride "row_tooltip" {
					tooltip = "nd_w_crisis_standdown_tt"
				}
				blockoverride "outcome_label" {
					text = "nd_w_crisis_standdown_label"
				}
				blockoverride "outcome_effect" {
					text = "nd_w_crisis_standdown_effect"
				}
				blockoverride "outcome_credibility" {
					text = "nd_w_crisis_cred_standdown"
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### Every nuclear crisis in the world (open; only while there is one), most
	### dangerous first: one row each (NUC-14), the issuer's flag, the
	### target's, the stage and the danger, the details on hover. Our own is
	### listed too, tinted, so the list is the whole world. Private warnings
	### are listed: the public may not know of one, but governments do (owner,
	### 2026-10-16). The rows are a datamodel over nd_crises, the issuers'
	### capitals nd_world_crises_refresh keeps on the panel's global store
	### (nuclear_crisis_effects.txt); nothing here sorts the world's countries.
	type te_nuclear_sec_world_crises = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 2
		visible = "[GetScriptedGui('nd_world_crises_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"

		nd_section_header = {
			blockoverride "left_text" {
				text = "nd_w_world_crises_header"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick" {
				onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Toggle('nd_world_crises_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
				visible = "[GetVariableSystem.Exists('nd_world_crises_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
				visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('nd_world_crises_closed'))]"
			}
		}

		nd_panel = {
			visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('nd_world_crises_closed'))]"

			nd_world_crisis_head = {}
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = vertical
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				spacing = 2
				datamodel = "[GetGlobalVariable('nd_lists_store').GetList('nd_crises')]"

				item = {
					nd_world_crisis_row = {
						datacontext = "[Scope.GetState]"
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### The posture in force (open; only while armed). Each of its three axes
	### is one row (NUC-3): the axis, a concept; what is in force, its hover
	### what it does now and when it can next change (NUC-4); and a Change
	### toggle that opens the axis's choices directly beneath it, collapsed by
	### default, each list under one live line saying when it can change. The
	### option in force is tinted (NUC-5); readiness is a comparison table.
	### Then the umbrella, loose warheads, upkeep and incident exposure.
	type te_nuclear_sec_posture = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 2
		visible = "[GetScriptedGui('nd_armed_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"

		nd_section_header = {
			blockoverride "left_text" {
				text = "nd_w_posture_header"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick" {
				onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Toggle('nd_posture_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
